{
  "name": "crane",
  "kind": "parts",
  "_about": "a common crane stalking: tall, ash-grey, the black neck and head with the white stripe from behind the eye down the neck, the red crown, a long dagger bill; the bustle of drooping dark tertials over the tail; long black legs (2026-11-08) The BILL is two sharp `horn`s (sharp.js): the upper mandible flat underneath with a keel, the lower flat on top, meeting along a crisp commissure in a true point. (2026-11-08) SLENDER NECK and LONGER BILL: the neck tubes thinner (4.9 cm radius at the base to 2.4 cm under the head, was 6.1 to 3.9; their blend .044/.022, was .044/.033) and the bill a long slim dagger (tip 19 cm ahead of the skull's centre, was 18 at a much deeper base; base 3.2 cm deep, was 5.3) the bill's root faired (horn `fair` .005) -- newbirds.py crane() and sharp/named.py. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
